Dear {{ recipient.salutation }},

I am writing as a Connecticut resident to ask that you protect the state's public pension fund from inappropriate exposure to private-equity and other high-risk strategies. The retirements of teachers, state workers, and many of my neighbors depend on the prudent stewardship of this fund.

Specifically, I ask that you publish quarterly disclosures of all alternative-investment holdings, including fees paid, and that you establish a clear ceiling on illiquid allocations.

Thank you for your attention to this matter.

Sincerely,


{{ writer.name }}
